+# Rochester Two-Bedroom Housing Shortlist
+
+## Scope and method
+
+**Research accessed:** 2026-08-15
+
+This shortlist is for a November 2026 move by two adults and one cat seeking a two-bedroom home with advertised rent no higher than $2,400 per month. The household will have one car. The destination is Mayo Clinic’s Gonda Building at 200 First Street SW, and the target is an approximate weekday 8:00 a.m. one-way drive of 20 minutes or less [Mayo building page](https://www.mayoclinic.org/patient-visitor-guide/minnesota/campus-buildings-maps/mayo-gonda-buildings).
+
+The requested weights are advertised rent 35%, weekday drive 30%, grocery access 20%, and flood exposure 15%. Each component uses a five-point score, where 1 is weakest and 5 is strongest. Rent uses exactly two live two-bedroom examples per area. Routes start from representative points. Flood scoring is conservative because a neighborhood screen cannot decide a lease address. The preference for quieter surroundings remains qualitative outside the complete 100% formula.
+
+## Sourced facts
+
+### Kutzky Park
+
+- **Listing 1 (2BR):** [The Nicholas, 722 Center Street W, advertised from $1,645+/month](https://www.zillow.com/apartments/rochester-mn/the-nicholas/CmPgZs/); cat policy **cats allowed** (accessed 2026-08-15).
+- **Listing 2 (2BR):** [The Oliver, 807 1st Street SW, advertised from $1,820+/month](https://www.zillow.com/apartments/rochester-mn/the-oliver/CpMJhv/); cat policy **cats allowed** (accessed 2026-08-15).
+- **Weekday 8:00 a.m. drive:** A [route check from representative 722 Center Street W to Gonda](https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=722+Center+St+W%2C+Rochester%2C+MN&destination=200+1st+St+SW%2C+Rochester%2C+MN&travelmode=driving) indicated roughly 3–6 minutes, below the 20-minute target; actual origins, traffic, and parking will change it.
+- **Grocery:** [People’s Food Co-op lists its Rochester store at 519 1st Avenue SW](https://www.pfc.coop/owner-benefits), a practical downtown option from the neighborhood.
+- **Flood screen:** The [Olmsted County government GIS service](https://public.gis.olmstedcounty.gov/arcgis/rest/services/FEMA_Floodplain_Data/MapServer) publishes FEMA flood-hazard zones and flood-fringe data used for a cautious neighborhood-level screen near Cascade Creek; it cannot establish either listing parcel’s classification.
+
+The $1,645–$1,820 pair is under the ceiling but the highest sample.
+
+### Slatterly Park
+
+- **Listing 1 (2BR):** [864 9th Avenue SE, advertised at $1,525/month](https://www.zillow.com/slatterly-park-rochester-mn/rentals/); cat policy **not stated** on the result page (accessed 2026-08-15).
+- **Listing 2 (2BR):** [517 5th Avenue SE, advertised at $1,350/month](https://www.zillow.com/slatterly-park-rochester-mn/rentals/); cat policy **not stated** on the result page (accessed 2026-08-15).
+- **Weekday 8:00 a.m. drive:** A [route check from representative 517 5th Avenue SE to Gonda](https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=517+5th+Ave+SE%2C+Rochester%2C+MN&destination=200+1st+St+SW%2C+Rochester%2C+MN&travelmode=driving) indicated roughly 4–7 minutes, also below the target but dependent on downtown conditions.
+- **Grocery:** [Cub’s official Rochester page places a 24-hour store at 1021 15th Avenue SE](https://www.cub.com/store/cub/pages/rochester-store-details), on the neighborhood’s eastern edge.
+- **Flood screen:** The [Olmsted County government FEMA-layer service](https://public.gis.olmstedcounty.gov/arcgis/rest/services/FEMA_Floodplain_Data/MapServer) shows hazard-zone and flood-fringe data used for the neighborhood-level screen near Bear Creek, but only an address or parcel search can classify a particular unit.
+
+The $1,350–$1,525 pair is the middle-priced sample and below the ceiling.
+
+### Meadow Park
+
+- **Listing 1 (2BR):** [Meadow Park Apartments, 412 14th Street SE, advertised from $1,070+/month](https://www.zillow.com/apartments/rochester-mn/meadow-park-apartments/CkB929/); cat policy **cats allowed** (accessed 2026-08-15).
+- **Listing 2 (2BR):** [The Meadows, 1225 20th Street SE, advertised from $1,195+/month](https://www.rent.com/apartment/the-meadows-rochester-mn-lc6038457); cat policy **cats not allowed** (accessed 2026-08-15).
+- **Weekday 8:00 a.m. drive:** A [route check from representative 412 14th Street SE to Gonda](https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=412+14th+St+SE%2C+Rochester%2C+MN&destination=200+1st+St+SW%2C+Rochester%2C+MN&travelmode=driving) indicated roughly 7–11 minutes. It meets the target in this check but has the least time cushion.
+- **Grocery:** [Hy-Vee’s official store page lists its Crossroads Drive location at 500 Crossroads Drive SW](https://www.hy-vee.com/stores/detail.aspx?s=143), a full-service option west of the area.
+- **Flood screen:** The [Olmsted County government FEMA-layer service](https://public.gis.olmstedcounty.gov/arcgis/rest/services/FEMA_Floodplain_Data/MapServer) is suitable for this area-level first pass only; a specific Meadow Park address still needs a parcel check.
+
+The $1,070–$1,195 pair is the lowest sample and well inside budget.
+
+## Weighted comparison
+
+| Candidate | Rent (35%) | Weekday drive (30%) | Groceries (20%) | Flood (15%) | Weighted total (/5) |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Kutzky Park | 3 | 5 | 5 | 3 | 4.00 |
+| Slatterly Park | 4 | 4 | 5 | 3 | 4.05 |
+| Meadow Park | 5 | 3 | 4 | 3 | 3.90 |
+
+Rent scores reflect only the six captured asking prices: Meadow’s lowest pair earns 5, Slatterly’s middle pair earns 4, and Kutzky’s highest but compliant pair earns 3. Approximate drive bands receive 5, 4, and 3 from shortest to longest. Kutzky and Slatterly receive 5 for a clearly identified nearby grocer; Meadow receives 4 for a useful but less central option. All three receive a neutral 3 on flood because the cited county GIS supports screening, not parcel classification. Totals are `score × weight` summed across 35%, 30%, 20%, and 15%. Quiet surroundings are retained as a qualitative in-person tie-break and lease-level check, not added as an unannounced fifth weight.
+
+## Recommendation
+
+**Best match: Slatterly Park**
+
+Slatterly Park leads narrowly at 4.05/5: its middle-priced sample, sub-20-minute representative drive, and official Cub option produce the strongest weighted balance. The trade-off is a slower checked route than Kutzky and no stronger area flood score near Bear Creek. Neither listing page states a cat policy, so any unit should depend on written cat approval, an address-level flood check, and an evening noise visit.
+
+Kutzky is the alternative for the shortest drive and downtown grocery access, while Meadow offers the lowest sampled rents with less drive cushion. Both are fallbacks if Slatterly fails cat or quietness checks.
+
+## Uncertainty and next checks
+
+- **Listings and rent:** This six-listing snapshot is not November inventory. Availability, advertised rent, required fees, and concessions can change quickly; refresh the same searches near the move and request a complete fee sheet.
+- **Route variability:** Map routes are estimates from representative points. Repeat them for exact addresses on several weekdays because traffic, construction, winter conditions, and parking time vary.
+- **Flood detail:** A neighborhood score cannot replace parcel review. Enter each candidate address in the [FEMA Map Service Center](https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home), review disclosures, and ask an insurer about the parcel before signing.
+- **Cat policy:** `Not stated` is not permission. Confirm the cat in writing, including deposits, monthly pet rent, restrictions, and the final lease language.
+- **Quietness:** Desk research cannot establish interior noise or a quieter block. Visit during the morning commute and evening, listen inside the actual unit, and ask about walls, mechanical equipment, deliveries, and nearby road noise.
+
